   "objective": "one logical full-scope run R7 of the candidate 1.10.0rc6 (every CSV row 0-27 as configured; not a pilot: --rows-first only orders the plan, reading rows 22, 27, 23 to 26 and 15 first, and --term-upc names the four product pages of the review; neither narrows the scope), two lanes, read in slices, each one ledger stage of the new credential's campaign oxylabs-marianos-20261116 whose ceiling is also set in the collector (set-ceiling). Every slice is ended by the operator with SIGTERM once the stage has its target of reservations (a resumable stop, exit 75); the ceiling, 10 above the target, is the backstop. Why R7: run R6 started at 23:40Z on 2026-11-16, when the site served page 1 again for 25 of 29 answers to a page 2 or later and for all 12 re-asks (measured by hour over all runs of the day: 10% at 03Z, 20-27% at 15Z, 28-34% at 16-17Z, 55-60% at 18Z, 80-86% at 23Z); a page has at most 2 re-asks in a run, so R6 was finalized offline after its first slice (rejected, never published) and R7 starts afresh in the night hours, with every page's re-asks intact. The envelope then held USD 4.7935 (3,195 submissions); a full run needs 3,145 to 3,750 submissions at F2's measured 1.43 per counted page, fewer at the night rate: if the envelope ends first, the run is left resumable after its last slice and the shortfall is reported with R7's measured rates. This slice starts the run and measures the hour's repeat rate before the larger slices.",
